The RAMB36E1 u_cpu_channel/u_package_fifo_cpu_rd/none_blk_mode.data_ram_dual.u_data_ram/gen_inferred_ram.gen_port_a_aligned.ram_reg has an input control pin u_cpu_channel/u_package_fifo_cpu_rd/none_blk_mode.data_ram_dual.u_data_ram/gen_inferred_ram.gen_port_a_aligned.ram_reg/ADDRARDADDR[10] (net: u_cpu_channel/u_package_fifo_cpu_rd/none_blk_mode.data_ram_dual.u_data_ram/D[7]) which is driven by a register (u_cpu_channel/u_package_fifo_cpu_rd/none_blk_mode.ram_addr_a_r_reg[7]) that has an active asychronous set or reset. This may cause corruption of the memory contents and/or read values when the set/reset is asserted and is not analyzed by the default static timing analysis. It is suggested to eliminate the use of a set/reset to registers driving this RAMB pin or else use a synchronous reset in which the assertion of the reset is timed by default.
